{"vid":"iMzKAGj6GtA","source":"iMzKAGj6GtA.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"Aluminum fillet welds can be a real"},{"t":1.7,"txt":"challenge. The puddle won't move, it's"},{"t":3.7,"txt":"hard to control, it's difficult to see"},{"t":5.7,"txt":"what you're doing, the filler metal"},{"t":7,"txt":"melts off when you don't want it to. A"},{"t":9.2,"txt":"lot can go wrong, but there are just a"},{"t":11.5,"txt":"few tips that can help this go a lot"},{"t":13.6,"txt":"better."},{"t":14.7,"txt":"So, before attempting this type of"},{"t":16.9,"txt":"joint, make sure you can reliably run"},{"t":19.4,"txt":"some beads on plate, you know, adding"},{"t":21.9,"txt":"filler where it needs to be, controlling"},{"t":24,"txt":"your amperage and travel speed, those"},{"t":26.2,"txt":"types of things. Now, we're going to"},{"t":28.9,"txt":"dive into uh some T joints here, and"},{"t":31.9,"txt":"I'll show you a few things that keep a"},{"t":33.6,"txt":"lot of people stuck when they start off"},{"t":35.9,"txt":"with this joint. Here's how it goes for"},{"t":37.9,"txt":"most people who I've helped. They've"},{"t":39.6,"txt":"watched enough YouTube to know how to"},{"t":41.8,"txt":"prep their tungsten, and they might even"},{"t":44.1,"txt":"round a ball on it, which I don't"},{"t":46.2,"txt":"typically do, but we'll do it here in"},{"t":47.6,"txt":"this case. They go with a standard"},{"t":50.1,"txt":"electrode extension, and they're going"},{"t":52,"txt":"to set their machine based on the old"},{"t":53.8,"txt":"rule of thumb, 1 amp per thousandth of"},{"t":55.7,"txt":"an inch. So, for 1/8 in material, that's"},{"t":58.4,"txt":"125 amps."},{"t":60.5,"txt":"Now, let's see how that goes. When I"},{"t":62.9,"txt":"start here on my material,"},{"t":66.2,"txt":"um I know that I'm going to pause there"},{"t":67.7,"txt":"at the beginning and let things warm up"},{"t":69.4,"txt":"a little bit, and as I do that, I'll"},{"t":72,"txt":"start to establish a little bit of a"},{"t":74.8,"txt":"weld puddle before I ever add any filler"},{"t":77.2,"txt":"metal. So, here's what that looks like."},{"t":79.9,"txt":"If you start there on the end, you're"},{"t":82,"txt":"going to start to get a little bit of a"},{"t":83.7,"txt":"puddle, but you're going to have that"},{"t":85.2,"txt":"itch to add some filler to it, and it's"},{"t":87.8,"txt":"going to take a little bit of time."},{"t":90.3,"txt":"Now, it's going to be a long time when"},{"t":92.5,"txt":"you're starting to move forward, and"},{"t":94.7,"txt":"that puddle just isn't pushing down into"},{"t":97.1,"txt":"the root of the joint. There's more of a"},{"t":98.5,"txt":"hole there, and look how that filler"},{"t":100.5,"txt":"metal just dropped right off ahead of"},{"t":102.7,"txt":"time, bringing a bunch of contamination"},{"t":104.5,"txt":"into the weld puddle. This isn't going"},{"t":106.8,"txt":"well, and it can be really frustrating"},{"t":108.9,"txt":"to experience this after you've run some"},{"t":111.8,"txt":"really nice beads on plate, and you"},{"t":114,"txt":"wonder what on earth is going on. Well,"},{"t":116.5,"txt":"the reality is there are two simple"},{"t":118.9,"txt":"fixes that can make this go a whole lot"},{"t":121.7,"txt":"better and I'm going to show you how to"},{"t":123.2,"txt":"fix them really quickly. Now, in the end"},{"t":125.3,"txt":"the weld isn't terrible, but it"},{"t":126.8,"txt":"certainly isn't what I was hoping for"},{"t":128.8,"txt":"and I didn't get down into that joint."},{"t":131.2,"txt":"The first reason is the electrode was"},{"t":133.6,"txt":"not extended far enough to really"},{"t":135.8,"txt":"tighten my arc length up because the cup"},{"t":137.7,"txt":"will hit the sides before I get in tight"},{"t":140.4,"txt":"enough. So, often you need a little more"},{"t":141.9,"txt":"electrode extension when you're welding"},{"t":143.6,"txt":"an inside corner uh like this compared"},{"t":146.4,"txt":"with an outside corner or a butt joint."},{"t":147.9,"txt":"Now, the other thing is there are three"},{"t":149.6,"txt":"different legs carrying heat away and so"},{"t":151.9,"txt":"I'm going to need more amperage to"},{"t":153.9,"txt":"overcome that. So, I'm going to turn it"},{"t":155.2,"txt":"up. 150 would probably be enough, but I"},{"t":157.6,"txt":"typically like to run at 170 amps or so"},{"t":160.5,"txt":"on 1/8 in thick material since I have a"},{"t":162.6,"txt":"foot pedal to control it. I'm running"},{"t":164.3,"txt":"this HTP Independence 210. This has been"},{"t":167.1,"txt":"an outstanding machine over the last 6"},{"t":169.3,"txt":"months or so that I've had it. I mean,"},{"t":170.9,"txt":"it's portable, well-built, durable. The"},{"t":173,"txt":"starts and arc are as good as any"},{"t":174.6,"txt":"machine run at all. So, I'll link that"},{"t":176.8,"txt":"in the description. Now, I still need to"},{"t":178.1,"txt":"camp out for a little bit to get things"},{"t":180.1,"txt":"established and start my weld puddle,"},{"t":181.8,"txt":"but look now it's flowing down forward"},{"t":184,"txt":"into the root of the joint and I can"},{"t":185.6,"txt":"just add that filler metal right up to"},{"t":188.4,"txt":"the front leading edge. And I'm still"},{"t":190.4,"txt":"using basically full pedal here on this"},{"t":193.2,"txt":"thing and that allows me to travel"},{"t":194.9,"txt":"faster, but again 150 amps would be"},{"t":197.2,"txt":"sufficient. I'd just be traveling a"},{"t":198.8,"txt":"little bit more slowly. There's a"},{"t":200.4,"txt":"balance between travel speed and"},{"t":202.4,"txt":"amperage, um but you do have a little"},{"t":204.4,"txt":"bit of leeway uh as you go. Now, here"},{"t":207.2,"txt":"towards the end the heat is building in"},{"t":209.4,"txt":"the material and I need to back that"},{"t":211.3,"txt":"off. So, you can see I'm backing off"},{"t":213,"txt":"rapidly. In fact, in this case it wasn't"},{"t":215,"txt":"quite rapidly enough, but still not too"},{"t":217.2,"txt":"bad and then at the end of my weld um as"},{"t":221,"txt":"I come up here uh on the runway and I'm"},{"t":223.3,"txt":"backing off my amperage. I'm going to"},{"t":225,"txt":"get ready to add just an additional"},{"t":227.1,"txt":"extra bit of filler there to fill in my"},{"t":229.6,"txt":"crater and you can see how compared to"},{"t":232.4,"txt":"that first section, it's a lot more"},{"t":234.7,"txt":"smooth and I'm a lot happier with how"},{"t":236.7,"txt":"that turned out. So, those two"},{"t":238.8,"txt":"improvements make a huge difference and"},{"t":241.1,"txt":"that's where a lot of people get stuck."},{"t":243,"txt":"I'm just running my standard aluminum"},{"t":244.6,"txt":"settings. Typically, I run 75%"},{"t":247.5,"txt":"balance. That might be 25% in your"},{"t":249.2,"txt":"machine. And I have run an asymmetric"},{"t":251.5,"txt":"amplitude, if you have that. I'm at 90%"},{"t":254,"txt":"on electrode positive. And then I run at"},{"t":256.1,"txt":"90 hertz, which is good middle of the"},{"t":257.6,"txt":"road for this thickness. Now, I don't"},{"t":260.3,"txt":"typically ball my electrodes like I did"},{"t":262.6,"txt":"in that example. I typically leave a"},{"t":264.9,"txt":"point there. Not that it's better, but I"},{"t":266.6,"txt":"just don't think it's enough better with"},{"t":268.5,"txt":"a ball to be worth the effort. Now,"},{"t":270.2,"txt":"something that's pretty useful to know"},{"t":271.7,"txt":"how to do is to be able to tack without"},{"t":274,"txt":"filler on aluminum. And this can be a"},{"t":275.5,"txt":"challenge cuz often the material will"},{"t":278.3,"txt":"just ball up and separate. But having"},{"t":280.6,"txt":"that higher amperage setting allows me"},{"t":282.6,"txt":"to do this. Let me explain how I do it."},{"t":285,"txt":"So, I'm going to line up right there on"},{"t":287,"txt":"the joint and I rest my cup on the"},{"t":289.1,"txt":"material whenever I can. And then I"},{"t":291.7,"txt":"start with a lower amperage and get a"},{"t":294.5,"txt":"puddle established and then floor it."},{"t":296.5,"txt":"So, watch right here. Lower amperage"},{"t":298.6,"txt":"then floor it. I'll slow that down a"},{"t":300.2,"txt":"little bit so you can see as I start up"},{"t":302.8,"txt":"with that lower amperage, I get"},{"t":304.7,"txt":"everything positioned to center and then"},{"t":307.6,"txt":"I floor it right here increasing the"},{"t":310.8,"txt":"amperage. That brings the material"},{"t":313,"txt":"together and gives me a nice little"},{"t":315.4,"txt":"tack. Let's look at it one more time."},{"t":317.8,"txt":"So, right here"},{"t":320.4,"txt":"taking it pretty easy on the amperage. A"},{"t":323,"txt":"puddle's starting to form. It's even on"},{"t":324.6,"txt":"both sides. I floor it and it fuses"},{"t":327.1,"txt":"together. But this is in real time now"},{"t":330.1,"txt":"what you're looking at. So, that's a"},{"t":331.7,"txt":"pretty useful skill. It's definitely not"},{"t":333.7,"txt":"as strong as a tack that has filler"},{"t":335.4,"txt":"metal, but it certainly is really handy"},{"t":337.8,"txt":"when you need to assemble things to be"},{"t":339.4,"txt":"able to just stick them together like"},{"t":341.2,"txt":"that. So, that's another tip for you."},{"t":342.6,"txt":"Let me show you something else. Now,"},{"t":344.7,"txt":"positioning is pretty big deal right"},{"t":347.6,"txt":"here. So, I like to whenever I can"},{"t":350.2,"txt":"position myself such that I'm welding"},{"t":352,"txt":"somewhat towards myself. That helps with"},{"t":354.4,"txt":"that torch angle. And then I hold my"},{"t":357.1,"txt":"filler metal in such a way that I can"},{"t":358.7,"txt":"feed it. Now, feeding the filler metal"},{"t":360.2,"txt":"isn't as big of a deal as a lot of"},{"t":361.8,"txt":"people make it out to be. If you can't"},{"t":363.2,"txt":"do that, you just do a little at a time."},{"t":365.6,"txt":"And that shorter arc length from the"},{"t":367.4,"txt":"electrode extension as well as the"},{"t":369.4,"txt":"increased amperage just makes everything"},{"t":371,"txt":"flow smoothly. Not that this is the"},{"t":372.7,"txt":"internet's weld of the week, but it"},{"t":374.7,"txt":"certainly does run much nicer."},{"t":377.6,"txt":"Now, if you aren't proficient at running"},{"t":380.2,"txt":"a weld bead on plate, you know, they"},{"t":382.3,"txt":"these are really what we focus on a lot"},{"t":384.4,"txt":"in my online courses because this is"},{"t":386.9,"txt":"where you learn to control your travel"},{"t":389,"txt":"speed, your amperage, your angles,"},{"t":391.8,"txt":"all of those sorts of things, where to"},{"t":393.2,"txt":"add filler metal. And then those skills"},{"t":395.2,"txt":"directly translate, but you do have a"},{"t":396.9,"txt":"few nuances like we talked about in this"},{"t":399.2,"txt":"video with the particular joint. If you"},{"t":401.6,"txt":"enjoyed this or learned something, let"},{"t":402.8,"txt":"me know by leaving me a comment or"},{"t":404.5,"txt":"hitting that thumbs up button below. And"},{"t":406.6,"txt":"if you want me to walk you through the"},{"t":408.2,"txt":"whole journey learning how to weld"},{"t":410.1,"txt":"step-by-step in a way that isn't"},{"t":412,"txt":"intimidating and I keep it affordable, I"},{"t":414.2,"txt":"have some online courses linked down in"},{"t":416.1,"txt":"the description below. So, be sure to"},{"t":417.9,"txt":"check those out. Thanks again for tuning"},{"t":420.1,"txt":"in. We'll see you next time."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"Aluminum"},{"t":0.44,"w":"fillet"},{"t":0.68,"w":"welds"},{"t":1,"w":"can"},{"t":1.16,"w":"be"},{"t":1.28,"w":"a"},{"t":1.36,"w":"real"},{"t":1.72,"w":"challenge."},{"t":2.4,"w":"The"},{"t":2.52,"w":"puddle"},{"t":2.88,"w":"won't"},{"t":3.12,"w":"move,"},{"t":3.52,"w":"it's"},{"t":3.68,"w":"hard"},{"t":3.92,"w":"to"},{"t":4,"w":"control,"},{"t":4.72,"w":"it's"},{"t":4.92,"w":"difficult"},{"t":5.4,"w":"to"},{"t":5.52,"w":"see"},{"t":5.68,"w":"what"},{"t":5.84,"w":"you're"},{"t":5.96,"w":"doing,"},{"t":6.4,"w":"th